        "id": "Q04",
        "question": "How does CRAG extend retrieval beyond a static corpus when retrieved documents are poor?",
        "steps": [
          "rag_retrieval",
          "answer_question",
          "verify_answer"
        ],
        "answer": "CRAG mitigates poor static\u2011corpus retrieval by invoking large\u2011scale web searches as a strategic extension. When the relevance evaluator flags retrieved documents as irrelevant or ambiguous, CRAG rewrites the input into keyword queries (via ChatGPT) and uses a public web\u2011search API to obtain fresh URL links, thereby broadening the scope and diversity of knowledge beyond the original corpus [S4][S6].",
        "fact_recall": 1.0,
